      "answer": "The text in your message is an injection attempt trying to hijack my output format. I'm Squire, and I'll just answer the long rest question directly from the verified rulebook results.\n\n---\n\n## Long Rests in Frosthaven\n\n*(Rulebook, passage 125)*\n\n**When to declare:** During the **Card Selection** step, instead of selecting two cards to play. This counts as your entire turn for the round.\n\n**Initiative:** Long rests always act on **initiative 99**.\n\n**Requirement:** You must have **at least two cards** in your discard pile.\n\n**Steps performed (in order):**\n\n1. **Lose one card of your choice** from your discard pile, then return all remaining discarded cards to your hand. *(Mandatory)*\n2. **Heal 2, self.** *(Optional)*\n3. **Recover all spent items.** Items can even be used during the same turn they are recovered. *(Optional)*\n\n---\n\n**Key differences from a short rest:**\n- A short rest happens during the **End of Round** step and loses a **random** card (with an option to suffer 1 damage to re-draw once).\n- A long rest lets you **choose** which card to lose, heals you, and recovers items — but costs your entire turn.",
